<speak>A short covering message is best. I do read the documents, but I dislike opening a long email to discover that the only thing I needed was hidden near the bottom. Tell me what the correspondence concerns, whether anything requires my attention, and where the full record is. That is how I am trying to get my own office to write as well. They sometimes send the entire history of a shipment when all I need is to know that a letter is waiting for my signature. I would rather have the history available than have it pasted into every message.</speak>